message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Exactly when 6H misses a move in the 547/727 prime race"
abstract: "The full set of late starting heights missing a move is determined for every completion factor at least six. The three sharp cutoffs and the exact integer census follow from prime arithmetic. The predecessor also gives a large-height obstruction under Dirichlet GRH."
